{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The assorted wood screws fit my repeated interest in fastening supplies and could complement the sizes in my existing kits.",
    "The ultrasonic cleaner felt useful for maintaining small hardware and repair parts, while the small syringes connected to my earlier adhesive, epoxy, and dropper-bottle purchases."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Breadboards, resistors, and printer filament require activities or equipment that my purchases do not establish; general DIY interest does not give me a reason to choose them now.",
    "The pressure gauge, pneumatic valve, pegboard hooks, and pocket-hole screws depend on particular fittings, equipment, or projects. Their usefulness remains uncertain even though they relate broadly to tools and workshop work."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "The recommendations seemed to treat interest in mechanical repair and fabrication as interest in almost any technical hobby supply.",
    "They also leaned too heavily on broad similarities such as measurement tools or screws without enough attention to what each item is designed to do."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My repeated purchases of rivets, rivet nuts, bolts, cutting supplies, and a grommet press suggest sustained interest in practical fastening and fabrication tasks.",
    "Compatibility and immediate usefulness matter: an adaptable assortment or a tool for caring for small parts feels more relevant than a specialized component with no established matching setup."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations recognized my hands-on repair interests but stretched them too far into unrelated equipment and specialized supplies without a clear use in my current work."
}"}
